      "id": "session:2026-10-15-4381279d",
      "type": "Session",
      "label": "Stale-graph reads, keeping the graph fresh, release 0.2.0",
      "description": "Goal: Resume the pasted plan: the stale graph first, then close v0.2.\nInstructions: The user pasted the previous plan; Claude recommended option 1 and then scrapy.\nDiscoveries: Letting hybrid read the files a stale graph reports lifts it from 0.63 to 0.83. Committing kg's own graph would conflict on almost every PR. The package version was still 0.1.0.dev0.\nAccomplished: Stale reads (#58); kg status --check and pre-commit hooks (#61), #59 closed; custom-type notes (#62), closing #18; Ask the graph in the README (#63), closing #40; #35 moved to v0.3 together with #55; #60 opened; v0.1.0 tagged; release 0.2.0 (#64) and its tag; v0.2 milestone closed.\nNext steps: Review the v0.3 order in docs/roadmap.md; step 3 of #52, scrapy, which decides whether v0.3 follows the table or starts a redesign.\nRelevant files: bench/tools.py, docs/store.md, README.md, docs/roadmap.md",
      "attrs": {
        "date": "2026-10-15",
